{
  "_readme": [
    "Hand-recorded facts about tax parcels, used by `ny-data-registry parcels` (issue #16, milestone 2). Reviewable: every value says where it came from.",
    "`state_layer` is the State's statewide public tax parcel service. Its endpoint is the one the NYS GIS Clearinghouse parcels page documents. It was read once, on the date below (epic #7, decision D3): one request for the service description, nothing else. The full response is kept in `evidence_file` (re-indented for review, otherwise unchanged).",
    "The counties that share their parcels are parsed from that response's serviceDescription by `parseStateParcelCounties` (src/parcels.ts), not typed by hand. The same 38 names are listed on the documentation page.",
    "`county_resources` is the 'County Parcel Data Resources (Revised May 2026)' table on the documentation page: the link the State gives for each county's own parcel data, viewer and extra resources. null means the page gives none ('NA'). These links were not checked.",
    "`registry_parcel_layers` was reviewed by hand on 2026-11-14 against the registry of 2026-11-13: each county row whose own registry text documents a parcel layer (a REST service that answers, or a download). `quote` is copied exactly from that row's `field`; a test checks it. A row that names only a viewer, a search page or a request form is not listed. Herkimer's layer is hosted on Oneida County's server."
  ],
